WEBVTT

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.380
I want all but one of you slimes to fall back.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:33.290
We're going to attack that dragon.

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:34.920
You got it!

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:40.080
Hellfire of Demise has more spread than we need.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.710
If that dragon's our only target...

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:45.040
<b>Sense Share</b>

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:45.040
<b>Sense Share</b>

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:45.040
<b>Sense Share</b>

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.040
<b>Weaknesses: Fire, Holy</b>

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.040
<b>Resistances: Earth, Wind, Water, Dark</b>

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.040
<b>Blue Dragon of Delight</b>

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:47.040
<b>Fire Magic</b>

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:47.040
<b>Hellfire of Decimation</b>

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:51.170
Spell-transfer: Hellfire of Decimation!

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:03.420
Yuji.

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:06.130
That didn't work.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.460
<b>Status</b>

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.460
<b>Blue Dragon of Delight</b>

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.460
<b>Resistances: Earth, Wind, Water, Dark</b>

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.460
<b>Weaknesses: Fire, Holy</b>

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:07.040
Brushing things off with a "whatever"

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:10.170
Stuck later in an unchanging life

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:12.420
The whatevers became habit

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:15.670
My skills still have yet to bloom

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:20.630
If I don't try to win and but am unwilling to lose

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:26.330
Why does this cold heart still beat with time?

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:32.630
All of us are monsters with hidden powers

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:38.500
Are we going to live without awakening them?

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:41.500
We push things down and cover them up

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:44.380
And our hearts are fresh no more

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:49.130
But we're monsters who continue on without so much as a face

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:55.540
All of us have undiscovered powers hidden inside

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:59.380
You're up next

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:05.080
Stand and face it monster

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:22.000
That blast packed quite a punch!

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:25.920
Did the dragon just get even bigger?

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:27.460
You're right!

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:30.830
Yuji!

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:33.250
Something's weird here.

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:46.170
Is it destroying this forest
to absorb more magical energy?

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:50.380
Yuji, what are we gonna do?

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:55.000
Our only choice is to fight.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:57.750
No way! With that dinky little thing?!

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.460
Are you serious?

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:00.420
Always.

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:03.750
<b>Unbreakable</b>

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:03.750
<b>Dagger of Kethis</b>

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:03.750
<b>A dagger of unknown origins.</b>

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:03.750
<b>Focuses the wielder's magic abilities</b>

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:03.750
<b>at the tip of its blade.</b>

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:03.750
<b>Blessed</b>

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:08.790
If I can take the firepower from a Hellfire of Demise blast
and concentrate it through this Dagger of Kethis,

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:10.790
it should deal a powerful blow.

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:15.080
We're going to slip in below that dragon!

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:26.250
That sure don't look good!

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:52.210
I do believe it's ready to blast us again!

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:56.880
We're counting on you!

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.920
No sweat!

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:01.040
Spell-transfer!

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:03.500
Spell-transferring Barrier!

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:09.210
Now's our chance to close in!

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:21.170
Sure is high up there...

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:24.290
A hearty 50 meters I reckon.

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:27.540
Jump Boost!

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:30.210
Anti-Physical Barrier! Jump Boost!

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:32.040
Anti-Physical Barrier! Jump Boost!

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:34.920
Look at him go!

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:41.750
Spell-transfer: Fireball!

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:53.500
Here goes.

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:00.460
Hellfire of Demise!

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:14.210
That takes care of that.

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:38.540
Probably would have died there if I let my guard down.

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:41.880
<b>Ice Magic</b>

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:41.880
<b>Master-class Magic  </b>

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:41.880
<b>Water Magic</b>

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:41.880
<b>Fire Magic</b>

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:41.880
<b>Spell Transfer             </b>

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:41.880
<b>Dark Magic</b>

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:41.880
<b>Holy Magic</b>

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:41.880
<b>Buff Magic</b>

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:41.880
<b>Yuji</b>

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:41.880
<b>Support Magic</b>

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:41.880
<b>Class: Tamer, Sage</b>

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:41.880
<b>Sense Share</b>

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:41.880
<b>Taming</b>

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:41.880
<b>Wind Magic</b>

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:41.880
<b>Lightning Magic</b>

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:41.880
<b>Taming Skills:</b>

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:41.880
<b>Combat Skills</b>

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:41.880
<b>Earth Magic</b>

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:41.880
<b>Type: None</b>

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:41.880
<b>Status Effect:</b>

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:41.880
<b>Excessive Magic Use</b>

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:41.420
Should have guessed that'd put my MP in the red.

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:43.830
Running low on HP, too.

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:06.500
All I need is one more hit.

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:10.170
But how am I going to draw it down here?

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:15.960
This isn't looking good.

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:18.290
<b>Buff Magic</b>

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:18.670
<b>Ice Magic</b>

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:18.670
<b>Permafrost Curse</b>

00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:18.670
This is going to be rough,

00:07:19.170 --> 00:07:21.000
but freezing it out of the sky is the only way!

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:25.420
<b>Divine Strike</b>

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:25.420
<b>Available in</b>

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:25.420
<b>seconds</b>

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:27.250
That'll be when I use it.

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:29.170
<b>Divine Strike</b>

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:29.170
<b>Available in</b>

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:29.170
<b>seconds</b>

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:29.080
This has got to be good for something.

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:41.330
It all comes down to this.

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:43.630
Divine Strike!

00:07:58.540 --> 00:07:59.460
Proud Wolf!

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:01.290
Coming right up!

00:08:11.540 --> 00:08:13.580
Got you now!

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:22.540
Hellfire of Demise!

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:38.290
We did it!

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:40.290
We won!

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:42.630
No one can beat Yuji!

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:45.540
We cut it a little close there...

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:48.750
Come on, let's head back to town.

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:50.000
Okay!

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:51.250
C'mon, move along.

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:11.380
Sorry to wake you so early.

00:09:12.380 --> 00:09:13.790
I stepped out for a bit last night.

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:17.000
The skies above Kilia have settled again.

00:09:17.670 --> 00:09:18.380
That so?

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:25.250
According to Father Steyl, the Blue Dragon
of Delight was defeated by a certain someone.

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:27.710
Why does the priest think that?

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:30.080
Says he heard it through the word of God.

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:31.710
Where is he now?

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:37.170
Already gone beyond the town boundaries.
Didn't mention where he was headed, either.

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:42.000
Yuji, all of us our sworn to protect the greater good.

00:09:42.210 --> 00:09:44.630
Remember you can rely on the guild when in need.

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:49.630
All you need to do is say,
"I'd like some help fighting a dragon."

00:09:50.630 --> 00:09:52.330
Why tell me this?

00:09:53.380 --> 00:09:54.460
Why indeed?

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:07.960
Sorry, Yuji.

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:12.040
Looks like the team I roped you into got disbanded.

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:14.790
Still, I'm glad we volunteered.

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:16.040
Mhmm!

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:17.790
Why's that?

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:23.670
Even though it got called off,
we still go down on record as joining up!

00:10:25.130 --> 00:10:27.460
Makes sense. They sure have their wits about them.

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:31.330
What are your plans now, Yuji?

00:10:31.670 --> 00:10:34.000
I'm thinking of moving on to another town.

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:40.080
Yeah? That's too bad,
but I guess that's the adventurer's life.

00:10:40.460 --> 00:10:42.670
Where you headed for, though?

00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:44.580
I wanted to talk with you two about that.

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:46.960
Anywhere you'd recommend?

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:51.040
How about Ricaardo?

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:52.460
Ricaardo?

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:56.830
Yup! That place has got the BEST eats.

00:10:57.290 --> 00:10:58.080
Really now...?

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:03.580
That's not a bad idea. It's a warm, comfortable place.

00:11:04.170 --> 00:11:06.040
Can I ask one thing, though?

00:11:06.380 --> 00:11:09.000
Nothing weird is going on there, right?

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:10.670
Weird like how?

00:11:11.630 --> 00:11:16.500
Like the sky changing colors, dragons showing up...

00:11:20.710 --> 00:11:25.330
Relax! Kilia's just been a bit off lately.

00:11:25.670 --> 00:11:29.750
If it was like this 'round here everyday
we'd all be dead forever ago.

00:11:31.170 --> 00:11:32.880
Guess we're headed for Ricaardo, then.

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:40.830
Bye-bye!

00:11:40.830 --> 00:11:41.540
See you around!

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:54.420
Yuji, I can't wait for dinner!

00:11:54.420 --> 00:11:55.790
For something yummy!

00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:57.210
Yummy, yummy dinner!

00:11:57.210 --> 00:11:58.130
Mmm, mmm!

00:11:58.790 --> 00:12:02.290
Probably best not to let people see my slimes in action.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:07.000
Yuji! We have an emergency!

00:12:08.420 --> 00:12:09.250
What's wrong?

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:12.330
Dryad's got an urgent message!

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:15.250
<b>Sense Share</b>

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:16.540
Yuji! Yuji! Come quick!

00:12:22.500 --> 00:12:25.500
The area where you fought off that dragon...

00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:30.170
...is now home to some really wonderful mushrooms!

00:12:31.380 --> 00:12:32.330
Mushrooms...?

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:39.000
I can't gather them all by myself, so I wanted your help!

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:41.920
That's fine and all, but what do you need them for?

00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:45.880
To fix up a really special potion!

00:12:46.330 --> 00:12:47.250
What for?

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:55.830
With these red dragon mushrooms,
I can make sage potions.

00:12:57.000 --> 00:13:01.250
And with the blue dragon mushrooms,
I can make mana restoratives!

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:03.420
And they restore what, exactly?

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:07.670
They bring your magic power back
to what it was ten minutes prior!

00:13:08.290 --> 00:13:09.500
Sounds useful.

00:13:10.460 --> 00:13:12.130
All right, I'll help.

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:15.880
Can I ask you to fix up some of those potions in return?

00:13:16.130 --> 00:13:17.580
Of course!

00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:20.130
Now, why don't we get started?

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:32.460
You're the best! That was so fast!

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:35.710
The slimes did all the work.

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:38.290
Think this is enough for those potions?

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:39.500
Yup!

00:14:00.630 --> 00:14:01.580
That does it!

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:03.670
But wait, this should have been a blue potion...

00:14:04.170 --> 00:14:06.540
Something's wrong with these mushrooms.

00:14:08.290 --> 00:14:10.880
They pack too much magical punch.

00:14:11.210 --> 00:14:18.040
I might still be able to fix some up
if we had crystal clear water.

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:20.330
Want me to try and distill some water?

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:22.460
Dis-what?

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:25.580
I changed up the shape of my barrier to act as a distiller.

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:32.420
If you boil the water to a vapor, then cool it back down
into a liquid, you're left with clean, clear water.

00:14:32.460 --> 00:14:34.080
<b>Tamer Skills</b>

00:14:32.750 --> 00:14:35.460
Then I can use Slime Purification on that water.

00:14:32.960 --> 00:14:33.830
<b>Slime Purification</b>

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:34.460
<b>Slime Purification</b>

00:14:34.210 --> 00:14:34.460
<b>Tamer Skills</b>

00:14:36.210 --> 00:14:38.880
Wow, I've never seen anything like this.

00:14:39.420 --> 00:14:41.290
It will take a while, though.

00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:46.750
That cloudy potion looks a lot like those magic stones.

00:14:47.210 --> 00:14:50.670
Now that I think about it, back when we first met...

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:05.380
Spell-transfer: Magic Conveyance!

00:15:09.750 --> 00:15:10.630
Are you all right?

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:13.790
I used my slime to transfer some of my magic to you.

00:15:15.630 --> 00:15:18.380
I feel better than ever! Thank you!

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:20.080
What happened?

00:15:20.710 --> 00:15:24.960
Someone left a magic stone
that drained away my power.

00:15:25.460 --> 00:15:28.040
My well-being is tied to this forest...

00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:32.830
Dispel Curse.

00:15:36.250 --> 00:15:37.250
Will that make things better?

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:42.210
Yeah... But something doesn't feel right.

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:46.670
Monsters?

00:15:47.290 --> 00:15:51.000
Spell-transfer: Anti-Physical Barrier! Anti-Magic Barrier!

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:52.580
Hellfire of Decimation!

00:15:57.330 --> 00:15:58.420
I don't believe it!

00:16:03.250 --> 00:16:04.540
Need help with anything else?

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:07.250
You've done plenty! Thank you!

00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:13.630
Take this as a little token of thanks.

00:16:19.420 --> 00:16:21.880
I owe you my life, after all!

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:28.290
Why does it look so much like those magic stones?

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:33.790
Well, the stones are probably fused with Dragon's Grace.

00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:35.420
What's that?

00:16:35.960 --> 00:16:40.080
A special sort of power that can only be found
at the site of a fallen dragon.

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:46.540
Its powerful magic is what
brings these potent mushrooms to life.

00:16:47.130 --> 00:16:48.540
And the magic stones use that power?

00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:49.540
Yeah...

00:16:50.790 --> 00:16:54.210
Dragon's Grace itself is neither good or evil,

00:16:54.790 --> 00:16:59.670
but if used in the wrong hands,
it can decimate entire forests.

00:17:00.380 --> 00:17:01.580
Yuji!

00:17:02.250 --> 00:17:03.500
All finished!

00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:14.080
It worked! It turned blue!

00:17:14.460 --> 00:17:15.580
That's all it took?

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:16.710
Yup!

00:17:17.420 --> 00:17:19.170
Thank you, Yuji!

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:28.710
Here are the sage potions
and mana restoratives I promised.

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:33.750
I'll be heading back to the Drya Forest.

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:37.630
All right. Let me know if you ever need anything else.

00:17:40.170 --> 00:17:41.710
Hope to see you again, Yuji!

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:48.710
This is quite the fog.

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:51.080
My good eye can't see a thing!

00:17:51.540 --> 00:17:54.790
We should make it to Ricaardo
if we keep heading this way.

00:17:56.080 --> 00:17:57.000
Hmm?

00:17:57.580 --> 00:17:59.880
I'm picking up some human-y scents.

00:18:00.170 --> 00:18:01.670
Way out here?

00:18:01.670 --> 00:18:03.880
Yeah. Gonna go take a look.

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:26.500
Think maybe this here's Ricaardo?

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:29.460
No, it should still be a ways off.

00:18:36.130 --> 00:18:38.210
Hmm? We've got company.

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:41.130
Looks like lotsa people live here.

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:45.130
What's everyone so smiley for?

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:47.500
Something's weird, huh?

00:18:53.040 --> 00:18:55.540
Greetings, traveler. Are you in need of something?

00:18:57.420 --> 00:19:00.920
Traveling through this fog is a dangerous errand.

00:19:01.290 --> 00:19:04.460
Care to spend an eve here with us to wait it out?

00:19:05.210 --> 00:19:07.710
No, I'll be making my way soon enough.

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:09.790
Is that so?

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:12.710
You might at least join us for a meal, then.

00:19:17.250 --> 00:19:19.670
Eat and enjoy.

00:19:22.460 --> 00:19:24.000
I don't mean to be rude, but I'm not hungry.

00:19:24.750 --> 00:19:30.380
Apologies if our meager offerings offended.

00:19:31.210 --> 00:19:33.460
Enlighten me, traveler.

00:19:34.290 --> 00:19:38.080
What business brings you to our tiny little village?

00:19:38.830 --> 00:19:39.790
Just happened on it.

00:19:40.580 --> 00:19:44.250
I was headed for Ricaardo, but the fog led me off route.

00:19:45.630 --> 00:19:48.040
You're certain that's all?

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:49.250
Quite.

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:52.000
Very well, then.

00:19:57.830 --> 00:20:03.960
My apologies. In our little village
we aren't accustomed to travelers.

00:20:04.920 --> 00:20:05.710
Right...

00:20:06.460 --> 00:20:07.830
I'll be making my way, then.

00:20:09.040 --> 00:20:11.330
What is this village called, anyway?

00:20:12.790 --> 00:20:14.920
This is the Village of Messias.

00:20:17.630 --> 00:20:21.500
Aww, so that wasn't Ricaardo?

00:20:21.750 --> 00:20:22.380
Nope.

00:20:22.750 --> 00:20:24.960
Food definitely didn't look yummy to me!

00:20:25.250 --> 00:20:27.460
No one's getting full on that!

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:29.460
The people were quite kind, however.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.130
Always smiling and stuff.

00:20:32.420 --> 00:20:34.790
Wonder what had them so happy.

00:20:37.670 --> 00:20:39.170
Something was definitely off about the place.

00:20:40.750 --> 00:20:47.880
Yes, a lone adventurer stumbled in on us,
but it was merely a tamer, so I doubt we need worry.

00:20:48.670 --> 00:20:51.130
Yes, our arrangements are in place.

00:20:51.920 --> 00:20:56.330
Tomorrow we will extract
the Dragon's Grace from Delight Canyon.

00:20:56.750 --> 00:20:58.500
You need not worry.

00:20:58.920 --> 00:21:00.210
If you'll excuse me, then...

00:21:00.790 --> 00:21:03.790
"Cleanse this tainted world!"

00:21:04.880 --> 00:21:07.670
We should make it to Ricaardo once we get over this hill.

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:09.960
The wait is over!

00:21:10.130 --> 00:21:12.460
Wonder what sorts of yummy meats they have.

00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:16.170
Maybe we can find a nice grassy place to rest and relax!

00:21:16.170 --> 00:21:18.170
Sounds like Heaven to me!

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:19.920
Ah! I think I've got eyes on it!

00:21:32.290 --> 00:21:34.960
This can't be normal...

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:41.000
<b>EPISODE 4</b>

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:41.000
<b>TRULY UNUSUAL SITUATIONS</b>

00:21:41.380 --> 00:21:43.710
Time to eat! Da da da dan!

00:21:43.960 --> 00:21:46.670
Exploration and procurement are our specialties

00:21:46.670 --> 00:21:48.130
"Be sure to bring lots of friends!"

00:21:49.130 --> 00:21:51.920
There's always an encounter one step away from town

00:21:51.920 --> 00:21:53.250
"Agh, I'm starved! My strength is gone!"

00:21:53.250 --> 00:21:54.710
"Look at all these tough baddies!"

00:21:54.710 --> 00:21:56.080
"This is ridic! Seriously ridic!"

00:21:56.080 --> 00:22:01.290
"Crazy, wild, and super glaring!"

00:21:56.460 --> 00:21:58.380
"Well it seems time we use our secret weapon!"

00:21:58.380 --> 00:22:00.000
"Since when do we have one?"

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:02.290
"I say we ruuun!"

00:22:01.290 --> 00:22:05.500
But we wound up surrounded

00:22:06.630 --> 00:22:10.920
We're about to experience annihilation!

00:22:12.670 --> 00:22:18.790
Brave heroes stand and fight!

00:22:18.960 --> 00:22:20.210
"Firepower boosting potions"

00:22:20.210 --> 00:22:21.290
"The more you chew, the more you get super healed"

00:22:21.290 --> 00:22:24.330
Strength strength coursing through us

00:22:24.330 --> 00:22:27.290
Here's some leaves!

00:22:25.670 --> 00:22:27.290
"Let's take them!"

00:22:27.290 --> 00:22:29.630
Time to eat! Da da da dan!

00:22:31.130 --> 00:22:36.130
This food we finally got our hands on is great, huh?

00:22:36.250 --> 00:22:38.880
Whether in caves or in the lost woods,

00:22:38.880 --> 00:22:41.880
Oh we eat our fill from nature's buffet

00:22:42.000 --> 00:22:46.920
Can't fight on an empty stomach!

00:22:47.040 --> 00:22:52.080
Let's go, give it a fusion attack! A super strong magical one

00:22:52.170 --> 00:22:55.170
Split the earth and breathe fire!

00:22:55.170 --> 00:22:56.580
"Ultimate super-powered magic!"

00:22:56.580 --> 00:22:57.960
"A jewelry box of magical power and cheats!"

00:22:57.960 --> 00:22:59.380
"Hellfire of Demise will get them all in one go!"

00:22:59.380 --> 00:23:02.170
"That was all in your dreams, right?"

00:23:01.330 --> 00:23:04.790
A CHEST!

00:23:02.170 --> 00:23:07.290
Yuji! Yuji! The best! The Sage! Yuji! Yuji! Oooh tame me!

00:23:07.290 --> 00:23:09.630
Time to eat! Da da da dan!

00:23:11.670 --> 00:23:14.080
Time for an isekai preview from us reincarnated slimes!

00:23:14.290 --> 00:23:16.210
Yikes, this place looks super cold!

00:23:16.210 --> 00:23:17.880
Not that it bothers us!

00:23:17.880 --> 00:23:19.210
What's "cold"?

00:23:19.210 --> 00:23:20.830
Things tend to freeze when its cold.

00:23:20.920 --> 00:23:22.130
What's "freeze" mean?

00:23:22.130 --> 00:23:24.580
When things freeze they turn hard.

00:23:24.580 --> 00:23:25.630
That sounds fun!

00:23:25.630 --> 00:23:28.130
We hardened slimes will smash through our foes!

00:23:28.130 --> 00:23:30.170
Let's beat up lots of baddies!

00:23:30.170 --> 00:23:33.000
We'd certainly be treated to a feast if we did!

00:23:33.000 --> 00:23:33.790
Yippee!

00:23:33.880 --> 00:23:34.710
Buuut...

00:23:34.460 --> 00:23:41.000
<b>THAT COLD LOOKED TROUBLING</b>

00:23:34.750 --> 00:23:36.920
"That cold looked troubling!"

00:23:37.080 --> 00:23:39.250
Wait, so cold is a bad thing?!
